[step] The condenser groove roof and corner-column pocket ceiling are independent 45-degree clearance faces. The groove keeps 0.25 mm of running clearance at the seated flange; the pocket follows its own room envelope. Their 0.75 mm Z/Y offset reads as 0.530 mm between parallel planes. Both faces rise toward the open insertion mouth and retain the full rail and column backing; the apparent step is the overlap of two open voids, not a thin load-bearing web.
