[ceiling] The front Z-slide heads' square catches stand at z=160.00 + 8.70 + 0.25 running clearance + 0.25 supported-face allowance = 169.20. Each overlaps the top's full-section foot and retains at least 3 mm of head stock. Lifting the seated top lands the flat foot on this face along the rail; its flat bearing resists lift without camming the seam open. The arm returns to the wall on its 45-degree under-flare, and slicer support carries the catch underside.
